 "result_text": "I fixed the duplicate `[None]` sections. I haven't run the tests or tried it against a real credentials file.\n\n**Cause:** when no profile is set (no `-p` and no `AWS_PROFILE`), `config.profile` is `None`. `_store` still wrote the credentials, and `RawConfigParser` turned that `None` into a section literally named `None`. The aws-cli parser then failed on the repeated section. I didn't trace exactly how the second run ended up with two of them.\n\n**Fix:** in `aws_google_auth/__init__.py`, `_store` is now called only when a profile is set. With no profile, the tool prints the `export` lines, as it already did, and writes nothing to disk.\n\n**Behavior change:** a run with no profile no longer writes anything to `~/.aws/credentials` or `~/.aws/config`. Before, it wrote a `[None]` section. If you'd rather write to a default profile such as `default` in that case, say so and I'll change it.\n\nAny `[None]` sections already in your credentials file will still make aws-cli fail until you delete them by hand.",
